+# Japanese kanji reading integration
+
+The local `3.0.2+romaji.1` build extends RefinedNowPlayingNext (MIT), based on
+https://github.com/SUlTlUS/refined-now-playing-netease-next at
+167bffe62b57bd276fc6aa34237c4a197f56fa7d. Its upstream identity/settings are retained.
+
+- Reading alignment and the patched kuromoji browser bundle are vendored unchanged
+  from https://github.com/Leleawa/jp-furigana at
+  b536d24b67a625dd4fc01a899e92da69a40cfb1f. Alignment code: MIT, copyright 2026 leleawa.
+  See `vendor/japanese/LICENSE`, `NOTICE.md` and `patch-kuromoji.js`.
+- kuromoji.js 0.1.2: Apache-2.0, copyright Takuya Asano and contributors.
+  The modified dictionary-loader hook is used to transfer local files to a Worker.
+  The complete license is in `vendor/japanese/LICENSE-kuromoji.txt`.
+- IPADIC binary dictionaries: the complete NAIST/ICOT copyright and disclaimer
+  are retained in `vendor/japanese/NOTICE.md` and in the distributed plugin.
+- WanaKana 5.3.1: MIT, https://github.com/WaniKani/WanaKana.
+  Its license is copied from the pinned npm dependency into the plugin.
+
+The integration adds a local Worker, bounds its cache, and renders annotations
+through React. It does not install or run jp-furigana's DOM observer plugin.
+No lyric text is sent to a third-party reading service.
